window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-8b62a89b49b84e46"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"manage-dots-permissions-and-capabilities\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"dots\">管理 dots（专属智能体）的权限与能力</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引见 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>dot 是 ChatGPT 中的个人智能体，可以承接持续性工作、使用已连接的应用，并把任务委派给 Work 或 Codex。管理员可以决定谁能使用 dots，以及它们能使用哪些功能；成员连接自己的账户，并告诉 dot 要处理什么工作。</p> <p>详细设置见<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001554-manage-dots-in-chatgpt-workspaces\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">在 ChatGPT 工作区中管理 dots（需联网）</a>；有关数据处理和审批的说明，见 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001529-dots-privacy-security-and-safety-faqs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">dots 隐私、安全与防护常见问题（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"find-what-you-need\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">查找所需内容</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>如果你需要……</th> <th>从这里开始</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>为某个群组开放访问权限</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46?anchor=set-up-dots-for-work\">为工作设置 dots</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>选择 dot 可使用的数据和工具</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46?anchor=2-configure-app-access\">应用访问权限</a>与<a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46?anchor=available-admin-controls\">计算机功能权限</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>设置 Slack</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46?anchor=3-configure-communication-channels\">Slack 连接方式与 dot 身份</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>了解后台工作与审批</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46?anchor=actions-and-ongoing-work\">操作与持续性工作</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>查看用量或调查某项操作</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46?anchor=models-and-usage\">模型与用量</a>以及<a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46?anchor=data-and-compliance\">数据与合规</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>某人转岗或离职时撤销访问权限</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46?anchor=manage-access-changes\">管理访问权限变更</a></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"set-up-dots-for-work\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"dots_1\">为工作设置 dots</h2> <p><a id=\"1-configure-role-based-access\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"1\">1. 配置基于角色的访问权限</h3> <p>工作区所有者通过工作区默认设置和自定义角色管理访问权限。若只想向特定群组开放 dots，请保持工作区默认设置为关闭，再将权限分配给这些群组。要检查成员被直接或通过群组分配的每一个角色：只要其中一个角色授予了访问权，在另一个角色中关闭权限也不会撤销它。</p> <p>请在<strong>管理控制台 &gt; 权限（Admin Console &gt; Permissions）</strong>中检查以下权限：</p> <ul> <li> <p><strong>使用 dots（Use dots）</strong>：允许成员使用 dots。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>将 dots 添加到 Slack 和 Microsoft Teams（Add dots to Slack and Microsoft Teams）</strong>：在相应渠道可用时，允许成员将自己的 dot 连接到受支持的消息渠道。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>允许访问本地计算机（Allow local computer access）</strong>：允许 dots 使用成员的本地计算机。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>使用 dots 自定义规则（Use custom rules for dots）</strong>：允许成员为自己的 dots 添加或编辑规则。</p> </li> </ul> <p>有关角色创建、分配及访问权限检查，参见<a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8?anchor=set-the-workspace-default-then-create-targeted-custom-roles\">基于角色的访问控制指南</a>。</p> <ol> <li> <p>打开<strong>管理控制台 &gt; 权限（Admin Console &gt; Permissions）</strong>。</p> </li> <li> <p>在“权限 &gt; 工作区默认设置 &gt; 工作区能力”（Permissions &gt; Workspace default &gt; Workspace capabilities）下，如果希望默认开放该能力，请启用“使用 dots（测试版）”（Use dots (Beta)）；否则通过自定义角色授予访问权限。</p> </li> <li> <p>设置 Slack 参与权限及 dot 自定义规则。本地计算机访问需要管理员单独选择启用；启用前请阅读<a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad?anchor=enable-local-computer-access\">本地计算机访问设置</a>。</p> </li> <li> <p>在<strong>允许智能体使用云端计算机（Let agents use cloud computers）</strong>下，根据组织策略检查是否允许<strong>使用浏览器（Use a browser）</strong>、<strong>允许网络访问（Allow network access）</strong>和<strong>允许使用计算机（Allow computer use）</strong>，以便浏览网站、访问在线服务和操作应用。工作区默认设置与自定义角色都要检查。</p> </li> <li> <p>在“工作区能力”（Workspace capabilities）下，根据工作区策略设置“使用密码管理器”（Use password manager）。</p> </li> <li> <p>保存，然后为一名预期使用该功能的成员检查访问权限。</p> </li> </ol> <p>启用 dots 时，如果相关云端计算机权限尚未启用，系统可能会提示你开启。dots、Work Cloud 和团队自动化共用这些权限。请只启用组织策略允许的功能。</p> <p>之后可前往<strong>管理控制台 &gt; 权限 &gt; 工作区默认设置 &gt; 工作区功能 &gt; 允许智能体使用云端计算机（Admin Console &gt; Permissions &gt; Workspace default &gt; Workspace capabilities &gt; Let agents use cloud computers）</strong>重新检查。访问本地计算机仍需单独选择启用。</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">dots 的“云端多做一些”权限提示，其中已启用使用浏览器、允许网络访问和允许使用计算机，并提示测试版的数据驻留与 Enterprise Key Management 限制。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dots/cloud-computer-permissions.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>dots 的“云端多做一些”权限提示，其中已启用使用浏览器、允许网络访问和允许使用计算机，并提示测试版的数据驻留与 Enterprise Key Management 限制。 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dots/cloud-computer-permissions.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>启用访问权限后，成员仍需完成 <a href=\"#/article/a-4b4aabd54f9e5c9c?anchor=slack\">Slack 设置</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-6e39401d1f472a38?anchor=connect-your-computer\">本地计算机设置</a>。他们此前已连接的受支持应用也可能供 dot 使用。</p> <p><span id=\"3-configure-approved-apps-and-actions\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"2-configure-app-access\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"2\">2. 配置应用访问</h3> <p>Dots 可以使用受支持的 ChatGPT 应用连接。配置访问权限时，请检查以下方面：</p> <ol> <li><strong>成员可以使用哪些应用。</strong>在<a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420\">插件控制</a>中设置可用应用和允许的操作。</li> <li><strong>已连接账户能访问哪些内容。</strong>检查该账户在来源应用中的权限。启用 dots 并不会自动让它访问所有共享云端硬盘、频道或文档。</li> <li><strong>哪些操作需要审批。</strong>某个应用即使已开放使用，其中部分操作仍可能需要审批。有关选项，请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001495-managing-app-permissions-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">应用权限（需联网）</a>。</li> </ol> <p>例如，允许读取文档，不一定也允许编辑或分享文档。若要限制对特定来源的访问，请检查已连接账户和应用权限。</p> <p><span id=\"4-choose-communication-channels-and-destinations\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"3-configure-communication-channels\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"3\">3. 配置通信渠道</h3> <p>成员可以通过以下两种方式将 Slack 连接到自己的 dot：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>设置方式</th> <th>成员体验</th> <th>管理员需要配置</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>通过 Plugins 连接成员自己的 Slack 账户</td> <td>成员在 ChatGPT 中与自己的 dot 对话；dot 可以使用其 Slack 连接，但没有独立的 Slack 身份。</td> <td>Slack 插件访问权限、已连接账户、允许的操作和审批。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>为 dot 设置独立的 Slack 身份</td> <td>所有者可以在 Slack 中私信或提及 dot；该对话中的其他人也能看到 dot 发布的内容。</td> <td>dots 消息权限、Slack 应用审批，以及每位成员对其 dot 的设置。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>关闭 dot 的 Slack 身份，不会撤销它通过成员已连接的 Slack 账户获得的访问权限。撤销 Slack 访问权时请同时检查这两种连接方式。成员设置步骤见<a href=\"#/article/a-4b4aabd54f9e5c9c?anchor=slack\">在 Slack 中向 dot 发消息</a>。</p> <p><strong>成员将自己的 dots 连接到 Slack 之前</strong></p> <ul> <li> <p><strong>ChatGPT 工作区所有者：</strong> 通过工作区默认设置或自定义角色，为预期使用的成员启用“使用 dots”和“将 dots 添加到 Slack 和 Microsoft Teams”。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>Slack 工作区所有者或应用管理员：</strong> 确保 Slack 中已经安装 ChatGPT 应用。如果工作区要求审批，请批准应用申请。参见 <a href=\"https://slack.com/help/articles/360024269514-Manage-app-requests-for-your-workspace\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Slack 应用审批指南（需联网）</a>。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>每位成员：</strong> 从 dot 的资料页将它连接到 Slack。参见<a href=\"#/article/a-4b4aabd54f9e5c9c?anchor=slack\">在 Slack 中向 dot 发消息</a>。</p> </li> </ul> <p>启用 ChatGPT 权限，不会在 Slack 中安装应用，也不会连接成员的 dot。</p> <p><span id=\"5-record-approval-and-oversight-responsibilities\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"manage-ongoing-work-and-access-changes\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"available-admin-controls\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">可用的管理员控制项</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th><strong>领域</strong></th> <th><strong>管理员能力</strong></th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>dots 访问</td> <td>通过工作区权限授予或撤销 dots 访问权限。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>云端及已连接的本地计算机</td> <td>控制“使用浏览器”“允许网络访问”“允许使用计算机”“使用密码管理器”及本地计算机访问。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>消息与参与</td> <td>启用或禁用 Slack 参与。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>已连接的应用</td> <td>通过<a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420\">插件控制</a>设置可用应用和允许的操作。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>dot 自定义规则</td> <td>禁用后，成员无法添加或编辑自定义规则，已保存的规则也不再生效。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>模型</td> <td>Enterprise 模型控制与默认设置不适用于主要 dot。请分别检查它委派给 Work 和 Codex 的任务。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><span id=\"can-we-use-o-if-our-workspace-requires-ekm-or-zdr\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"does-background-work-count-toward-usage-limits\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"enterprise-availability-and-limitations\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"review-availability-and-data-requirements\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">检查可用性与数据要求</h2> <p>启用 dots 前，请查看帮助中心的<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001530-getting-started-with-your-dot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">开始使用你的 dot（需联网）</a>以及工作区设置期间显示的提示。如果组织要求数据驻留、推理驻留、Enterprise Key Management（企业密钥管理）或特定合规范围，请在开放访问前向客户团队确认 dots 是否受支持。</p> <p>分别确认 dot 本身、它委派给 Work 或 Codex 的任务，以及连接的计算机所适用的要求。有关云端浏览器、网络和计算机使用，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-eea2edbcef587cb2\">云端安全</a>；有关员工设备上的操作，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad\">本地计算机访问</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"dots-faq\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"dots_2\">Dots 常见问题</h2> <p><a id=\"access-and-eligibility\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">访问与适用资格</h3> <p><span id=\"does-access-to-o-grant-access-to-apps-and-websites\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"dots\"></a> <strong>获得 dots 访问权限，就能访问应用和网站吗？</strong></p> <p>不能。dots 访问权限不会授予应用或网站访问权限。应用连接需要授权；网站上的工作使用浏览器中已登录的账户。</p> <p><span id=\"whose-account-does-o-use-for-connected-work\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"dot\"></a> <strong>dot 通过连接开展工作时，使用谁的账户？</strong></p> <p>对于应用，dot 使用已连接的账户；对于网站，它使用云端浏览器中已登录的账户。请分别检查两个账户的权限。参见<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001494-connecting-and-managing-app-accounts-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">管理应用账户（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><span id=\"can-o-use-a-local-computer-vpn-or-existing-sign-in\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"dot-vpn\"></a> <strong>dot 能使用本地计算机、VPN 或现有登录状态吗？</strong></p> <p>dot 的云端计算机与成员的本地计算机相互独立。本地工作需要一台已连接且在线的计算机，并且 ChatGPT 保持打开、访问权限已启用。本地登录状态、VPN 访问和设备策略不会自动延伸到云端计算机。</p> <p><span id=\"can-we-use-o-with-policies-that-target-an-operating-system\"></span></p> <p><strong>云端策略如何影响本地计算机访问？</strong></p> <p>如果任何一项云端策略启用了 <code>enforce_residency</code>，dots 就无法访问本地计算机；Work Cloud 仍然可用。有关策略要求，参见<a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad?anchor=check-data-handling-and-the-local-access-safeguard\">本地访问保护措施</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"actions-and-ongoing-work\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">操作与持续性工作</h3> <p><span id=\"can-o-keep-working-when-the-user-is-away\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"dot-1\"></a> <strong>用户不在时，dot 能继续工作吗？</strong></p> <p>可以。成员可以分配<a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2?anchor=assigned-work\">持续性职责</a>。工作区权限和审批规则仍然适用。本地工作需要计算机保持在线，ChatGPT 保持打开，且访问权限已启用。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2?anchor=proactive-research\">主动研究</a>使用受限工具读取已连接的应用。它不能发送消息、更改内容或控制浏览器和计算机。若要根据发现采取行动，dot 需要获得用户授权，并具备所需权限及审批。</p> <p><a id=\"dot-2\"></a> <strong>谁可以向 dot 发消息或看到它的结果？</strong></p> <p>只有所有者可以通过 Slack 私信或受支持渠道中的提及来指挥自己的 dot。其他人的消息不会启动工作。</p> <p>当所有者将 dot 带入 Slack 讨论串时，它可以将其他参与者的消息作为上下文。任何拥有该对话访问权限的人都能看到它的帖子。跨渠道携带的上下文并不授权将内容分享给新的受众；发布工作内容前请检查接收者。</p> <p>Microsoft Teams 访问仅限受邀参加 alpha（早期测试）的用户。</p> <p><span id=\"does-o-always-ask-before-sending-or-changing-something\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"dot-3\"></a> <strong>dot 在发送或更改内容前，一定会先询问吗？</strong></p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-e13354c6b025f6aa?anchor=how-action-review-works\">自动审查</a>会依据用户指令、自定义规则及安全要求检查拟执行的操作。让 dot 起草消息，并不表示授权它发送消息。有关审批选项，参见<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001495-managing-app-permissions-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">应用权限（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><span id=\"how-should-we-stop-work-or-remove-a-users-access\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"dots-1\"></a> <strong>管理员如何撤销 dots 访问权限？</strong></p> <p>有关撤销访问权限以及检查已连接账户、计算机和持续性工作的步骤，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46?anchor=manage-access-changes\">管理访问权限变更</a>。</p> <p><span id=\"how-do-custom-rules-affect-confirmations\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"-1\"></a> <strong>自定义规则如何影响确认？</strong></p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-e13354c6b025f6aa?anchor=set-custom-rules\">dot 自定义规则</a>用于指导 dot 何时行动或请求确认。关闭规则后，成员无法添加或编辑规则，已保存的规则也不再生效；dot 仍会遵循默认规则和用户指令。</p> <p>自定义规则不会授予工具访问权，也不能覆盖工作区权限或内置安全要求。关闭规则也不意味着 dot 会在每项操作前都询问。请通过功能权限和应用审批设置控制它可以执行的操作。</p> <p><span id=\"what-safeguards-help-protect-work-done-by-dots\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"dots-2\"></a> <strong>哪些防护措施有助于保护 dots 执行的工作？</strong></p> <p>内置防护措施有助于抵御恶意指令；当监测发现安全问题时，可以暂停或停止工作。</p> <p>成员可以在<a href=\"#/article/a-e13354c6b025f6aa?anchor=review-work\">活动视图</a>中跟踪进度、调整工作方向，并在使用结果前进行检查。</p> <p><a id=\"models-and-usage\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">模型与用量</h3> <p><span id=\"do-existing-model-controls-and-defaults-apply-to-o\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"dots-3\"></a> <strong>现有模型控制与默认设置适用于 dots 吗？</strong></p> <p>Enterprise 模型控制与默认设置不适用于主要 dot。它委派给 Work 或 Codex 的任务则遵循相应产品的权限和控制措施。配置访问权限时，请分别检查 dots、Work 和 Codex 的设置。</p> <p><a id=\"-2\"></a> <strong>管理员应如何监测采用情况与用量？</strong></p> <p>使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-88b1ced5fbccd242\">Analytics API（分析 API）</a>查看哪些人在使用 dots。dot 启动或管理的 Work、Codex 任务会计入这些产品的用量限额，并显示在相应报告中。审查用量时也要计入这些任务；制定预算时请核对当前套餐条款。可用的控制项见 <a href=\"#/article/a-ba100f6664b7be87\">Work 用量与费用</a>。</p> <p>每日用量端点 <code>/v1/analytics/workspaces/{workspace_id}/usage</code> 会用 <code>client_id = DOTS</code> 标识 dots，并支持按用户或工作区汇总报告。</p> <p><span id=\"which-data-policies-should-we-review-for-o\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"data-and-compliance\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_7\">数据与合规</h3> <p>默认情况下，OpenAI 不会使用 ChatGPT Enterprise 数据来改进模型。有关 OpenAI 的企业数据承诺，参见<a href=\"https://openai.com/enterprise-privacy/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">企业隐私（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><span id=\"what-does-o-remember-between-requests\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"dot-4\"></a> <strong>在不同请求之间，dot 会记住什么？</strong></p> <p>dot 会保留自己的上下文，与 ChatGPT 记忆分开。关闭 ChatGPT 记忆会停止向 dot 分享记忆，但不会删除 dot 已经获得的信息。断开插件只会停止它今后通过该连接访问内容，不会移除 dot 已留存的信息。</p> <p>删除 dot 会移除它自己的上下文；但它创建的文件、Codex 对话线程和 ChatGPT 对话分别存储，不会随 dot 一并全部删除。需要清理时，请按各自位置的删除流程操作。</p> <p>有关保留与删除哪些信息，请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001529-dots-privacy-security-and-safety-faqs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">dots 隐私常见问题（需联网）</a>；有关成员可用的“暂停”和“重置”控制，请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001530-getting-started-with-your-dot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">开始使用你的 dot（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><span id=\"how-can-admins-investigate-work-o-has-done\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"dot-5\"></a> <strong>管理员如何调查 dot 已完成的工作？</strong></p> <p>成员可以在“活动视图”中跟踪 dot 的工作。管理员可以使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0?anchor=confirm-the-administration-boundaries\">Compliance API（合规 API）</a>记录调查用户消息和 dots 的回复。在依赖导出数据开展审计、数据防泄漏（DLP）、法律保全或电子取证之前，请先确认实际提供了哪些记录。</p> <p>合规日志平台（Compliance Logs Platform）提供受支持的 dots 记录，包括用户提示词和回复、受支持的工具调用事件，以及已连接应用的 MCP 调用和结果。记录会标明用户和工作区；归属于 dots 的记录使用 <code>client_id = DOTS</code>，并且在有数据时，智能体对象会包含 dot 的 ID、名称和类型。</p> <p>工作区所有者或管理员可在管理控制台选择工作区，然后打开<strong>凭据 &gt; 管理员密钥（Credentials &gt; Admin keys）</strong>，创建具有相应可用权限的密钥：统一用量报告使用 <code>enterprise.analytics.usage.read</code>；dots 合规记录使用 <code>CODEX_LOG</code>。在支持的情况下，只有工作区所有者可以授予广泛的合规访问权限或<strong>对话消息（Conversation messages）</strong>访问权限。使用<a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/public/admin/api-reference\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">管理员 API 参考（需联网）</a>列出并下载合规 JSONL 文件，再筛选 <code>client_id = DOTS</code> 的记录。</p> <p><a id=\"manage-access-changes\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">管理访问权限变更</h2> <p>当成员转岗或离开时，请检查其 dot 的权限、连接和持续性工作：</p> <ol> <li><strong>撤销 dots 访问权限。</strong>检查工作区默认设置，以及直接分配或通过群组分配给该成员的每个角色。移除所有授予访问权限的项目；只要还有一项授权，访问权限就可能仍然开启。</li> <li><strong>检查已连接的账户和设备。</strong>检查插件授权、网站会话、本地计算机访问权限和 dot 的 Slack 身份；这些设置彼此独立。</li> <li><strong>决定如何处理持续性工作。</strong>检查正在执行的任务、定期计划，以及委派给 Work 或 Codex 的任务；决定哪些要停止、剩余职责由谁接手。</li> <li><strong>按需删除数据。</strong>撤销访问权与删除数据是两个独立步骤。请分别按 dot 上下文以及其他位置所存文件或任务的删除流程处理。</li> </ol> <p>有关添加和移除工作区成员的信息，参见<a href=\"#/article/a-16cf27f48eb09b1c\">用户生命周期管理</a>。有关撤销 dots 访问权限，参见<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001554-manage-dots-in-chatgpt-workspaces\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">在 ChatGPT 工作区中管理 dots（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"respond-to-an-unexpected-action\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">应对意外操作</h3> <p>请成员先暂停 dot，并检查受影响的任务。保存任务链接和现有活动记录，检查涉及的应用或计算机权限，并遵循组织的事件处理流程。能否撤销操作取决于具体操作和服务。有关问题报告方式，请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001529-dots-privacy-security-and-safety-faqs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">隐私与安全常见问题（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"help-members-work-well-with-dots\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"dots_3\">帮助成员更好地使用 dots</h2> <p>帮助成员选择适合委派的工作，并连接所需账户和工具。提醒他们告诉 dot 要做什么、何时做，以及结果应提供给谁。</p> <p>例如，“为我准备一份每周项目进度，先让我审核”是在要求草拟内容；“每周五把已批准的进度发布到团队频道”则同时授权发布。成员应检查重要结果，并了解如何查看活动、修改计划和暂停 dot。可以分享<a href=\"#/article/a-7c8e52e0c73fc7d7\">开始使用</a>、<a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2\">任务与记忆</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-e13354c6b025f6aa\">控制项</a>，帮助成员入门。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"manage-dots-permissions-and-capabilities\">Manage dots permissions and capabilities</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>A dot is a personal agent in ChatGPT that can take on ongoing work, use connected apps, and delegate tasks to Work or Codex. You choose who can use dots and which capabilities they can access. Members connect their accounts and tell their dots what to work on.</p> <p>For detailed settings, see <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001554-manage-dots-in-chatgpt-workspaces\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Manage dots in ChatGPT workspaces (online)</a>. The <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001529-dots-privacy-security-and-safety-faqs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">privacy, security, and safety FAQ (online)</a> covers data handling and approvals.</p> <h2 id=\"find-what-you-need\">Find what you need</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>If you need to…</th> <th>Start here</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Give a group access</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46?anchor=set-up-dots-for-work\">Set up dots for work</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Choose which data and tools a dot can use</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46?anchor=2-configure-app-access\">App access</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46?anchor=available-admin-controls\">computer capabilities</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Set up Slack</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46?anchor=3-configure-communication-channels\">Slack connections and dot identities</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Understand background work and approvals</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46?anchor=actions-and-ongoing-work\">Actions and ongoing work</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Track usage or investigate an action</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46?anchor=models-and-usage\">Models and usage</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46?anchor=data-and-compliance\">Data and compliance</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Remove access when someone changes roles or leaves</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46?anchor=manage-access-changes\">Manage access changes</a></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"set-up-dots-for-work\">Set up dots for work</h2> <h3 id=\"1-configure-role-based-access\">1. Configure role-based access</h3> <p>Workspace owners manage access through workspace defaults and custom roles. To give selected groups access, keep the workspace default off and assign a custom role to those groups. Check every role assigned to a member: if one role grants access, turning it off in another role won't remove it.</p> <p>Review these permissions in <strong>Permissions</strong>:</p> <ul> <li> <p><strong>Use dots</strong>: Allow members to use dots.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>Add dots to Slack and Microsoft Teams</strong>: Allow members to connect their dots to supported messaging channels where available.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>Allow local computer access</strong>: Allow dots to use a member’s local computer.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>Use custom rules for dots</strong>: Allow members to add or edit rules for their dots.</p> </li> </ul> <p>For role creation, assignment, and access checks, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8?anchor=set-the-workspace-default-then-create-targeted-custom-roles\">role-based access control guide</a>.</p> <ol> <li> <p>Open <strong>Admin Console</strong> &gt; <strong>Permissions</strong>.</p> </li> <li> <p>Under Permissions &gt; Workspace default &gt; Workspace capabilities, enable Use dots (Beta) if it should be available by default; otherwise grant access through a custom role.</p> </li> <li> <p>Set Slack participation and custom dot rules. Local computer access requires a separate admin opt-in; review <a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad?anchor=enable-local-computer-access\">local computer access setup</a> before enabling it.</p> </li> <li> <p>Under <strong>Let agents use cloud computers</strong>, review <strong>Use a browser</strong>, <strong>Allow network access</strong>, and <strong>Allow computer use</strong> where your policies allow browsing websites, accessing online services, and interacting with apps. Review both workspace defaults and custom roles.</p> </li> <li> <p>Under Workspace capabilities, set Use password manager according to your workspace policy.</p> </li> <li> <p>Save, then check access for an intended member.</p> </li> </ol> <p>When you enable dots, you may be asked to turn on cloud computer capabilities that are still off. Dots, Work Cloud, and team automations share these permissions. Choose the capabilities your organization's policies allow.</p> <p>To review them later, go to <strong>Admin Console</strong> &gt; <strong>Permissions</strong> &gt; <strong>Workspace default</strong> &gt; <strong>Workspace capabilities</strong> &gt; <strong>Let agents use cloud computers</strong>. Local computer access is a separate opt-in.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Do more with dots permission prompt with Use a browser, Allow network access, and Allow computer use enabled, plus a notice about beta residency and Enterprise Key Management limitations. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dots/cloud-computer-permissions.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Do more with dots permission prompt with Use a browser, Allow network access, and Allow computer use enabled, plus a notice about beta residency and Enterprise Key Management limitations. · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/dots/cloud-computer-permissions.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>Members still need to complete <a href=\"#/article/a-4b4aabd54f9e5c9c?anchor=slack\">Slack</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-6e39401d1f472a38?anchor=connect-your-computer\">local-computer setup</a> after you enable access. Supported app connections they've already set up may be available to their dot.</p> <p><span id=\"3-configure-approved-apps-and-actions\"></span></p> <h3 id=\"2-configure-app-access\">2. Configure app access</h3> <p>Dots can use supported ChatGPT app connections. When setting up access, check:</p> <ol> <li><strong>Which apps members can use.</strong> Set available apps and allowed actions in <a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420\">Plugin controls</a>.</li> <li><strong>What the connected account can access.</strong> Check the account's permissions in the source app. Enabling dots doesn't give it access to every shared drive, channel, or document.</li> <li><strong>When approval is required.</strong> An app can be available while some actions still need approval. See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001495-managing-app-permissions-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">app permissions (online)</a> for the options.</li> </ol> <p>For example, permission to read a document may not include editing or sharing it. To restrict access to a particular source, check the connected account and app permissions.</p> <p><span id=\"4-choose-communication-channels-and-destinations\"></span></p> <h3 id=\"3-configure-communication-channels\">3. Configure communication channels</h3> <p>Members can connect Slack to their dot in two ways:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Setup</th> <th>Member experience</th> <th>What to configure</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Connect the member’s Slack account through Plugins</td> <td>Members talk to their dot in ChatGPT. It can use their Slack connection without having its own Slack identity.</td> <td>Slack plugin access, the connected account, allowed actions, and approvals.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Give the dot its own Slack identity</td> <td>The owner can message or mention the dot in Slack, and its posts are visible to people in that conversation.</td> <td>Dots messaging permission, Slack app approval, and each member’s dot setup.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Turning off a dot's Slack identity doesn't remove its access through the member's connected Slack account. Check both when removing Slack access. For member setup, see <a href=\"#/article/a-4b4aabd54f9e5c9c?anchor=slack\">Messaging</a>.</p> <p><strong>Before members connect their dots to Slack</strong></p> <ul> <li> <p><strong>ChatGPT workspace owner:</strong> Enable Use dots and Add dots to Slack and Microsoft Teams for the intended members through workspace defaults or custom roles.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>Slack workspace owner or app manager:</strong> Ensure the ChatGPT app is installed in Slack. Approve app requests if required by your workspace. See <a href=\"https://slack.com/help/articles/360024269514-Manage-app-requests-for-your-workspace\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Slack’s app approval guidance (online)</a>.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>Each member:</strong> Connect your dot to Slack from its profile. See <a href=\"#/article/a-4b4aabd54f9e5c9c?anchor=slack\">Message your dot in Slack</a>.</p> </li> </ul> <p>Enabling the ChatGPT permission does not install an app in Slack or connect a member’s dot.</p> <p><span id=\"5-record-approval-and-oversight-responsibilities\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"manage-ongoing-work-and-access-changes\"></span></p> <h2 id=\"available-admin-controls\">Available admin controls</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th><strong>Area</strong></th> <th><strong>Admin capability</strong></th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Access to dots</td> <td>Grant or revoke dots access through workspace permissions.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Cloud and connected local computers</td> <td>Control Use a browser, Allow network access, Allow computer use, Use password manager, and local-computer access.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Messaging and participation</td> <td>Enable or disable Slack participation.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Connected apps</td> <td>Set available apps and allowed actions through <a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420\">Plugin controls</a>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Custom dot rules</td> <td>When disabled, members cannot add or edit custom rules, and saved rules do not apply.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Models</td> <td>Enterprise model controls and defaults do not apply to the main dot. Review delegated Work and Codex tasks separately.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><span id=\"can-we-use-o-if-our-workspace-requires-ekm-or-zdr\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"does-background-work-count-toward-usage-limits\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"enterprise-availability-and-limitations\"></span></p> <h2 id=\"review-availability-and-data-requirements\">Review availability and data requirements</h2> <p>Before enabling dots, review current availability in <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001530-getting-started-with-your-dot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Getting started with your dot (online)</a> and the workspace notices shown during setup. If your organization requires data or inference residency, Enterprise Key Management, or specific compliance coverage, confirm support for dots with your account team before enabling access.</p> <p>Check requirements for the dot itself, tasks it delegates to Work or Codex, and any connected computer. For cloud browser, network, and computer use, see <a href=\"#/article/a-eea2edbcef587cb2\">cloud security</a>. For work on employee devices, see <a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad\">local computer access</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"dots-faq\">Dots FAQ</h2> <h3 id=\"access-and-eligibility\">Access and eligibility</h3> <p><span id=\"does-access-to-o-grant-access-to-apps-and-websites\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"does-access-to-dots-grant-access-to-apps-and-websites\"></a> <strong>Does access to dots grant access to apps and websites?</strong></p> <p>No. Dots access does not grant access to apps or websites. App connections require authorization; website work uses the browser’s signed-in account.</p> <p><span id=\"whose-account-does-o-use-for-connected-work\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"whose-account-does-a-dot-use-for-connected-work\"></a> <strong>Whose account does a dot use for connected work?</strong></p> <p>For apps, a dot uses the connected account. For websites, it uses the account signed in to the cloud browser. Check the permissions for each account. See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001494-connecting-and-managing-app-accounts-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Managing app accounts (online)</a>.</p> <p><span id=\"can-o-use-a-local-computer-vpn-or-existing-sign-in\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"can-a-dot-use-a-local-computer-vpn-or-existing-sign-in\"></a> <strong>Can a dot use a local computer, VPN, or existing sign-in?</strong></p> <p>A dot’s cloud computer is separate from a member’s local computer. Local work requires a connected, online computer with ChatGPT open and access enabled. Local sign-in, VPN access, and device policies do not automatically extend to the cloud computer.</p> <p><span id=\"can-we-use-o-with-policies-that-target-an-operating-system\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"how-do-cloud-policies-affect-local-computer-access\"></a> <strong>How do cloud policies affect local computer access?</strong></p> <p>If any cloud policy has <code>enforce_residency</code> enabled, local computer access is unavailable for dots. Work Cloud remains available. See the <a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad?anchor=check-data-handling-and-the-local-access-safeguard\">local-access safeguard</a> for the policy requirements.</p> <h3 id=\"actions-and-ongoing-work\">Actions and ongoing work</h3> <p><span id=\"can-o-keep-working-when-the-user-is-away\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"can-a-dot-keep-working-when-the-user-is-away\"></a> <strong>Can a dot keep working when the user is away?</strong></p> <p>Yes. Members can assign <a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2?anchor=assigned-work\">ongoing responsibilities</a>. Workspace permissions and approval rules still apply. Local work requires the computer to stay online with ChatGPT open and access enabled.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2?anchor=proactive-research\">Proactive research</a> uses restricted tools to read connected apps. It cannot send messages, change content, or control a browser or computer. To act on what it finds, the dot needs the user's authorization and the required permissions and approvals.</p> <p><a id=\"who-can-message-a-dot-or-see-its-results\"></a> <strong>Who can message a dot or see its results?</strong></p> <p>Only the owner can direct their dot through a Slack direct message or supported channel mention. Messages from other people do not start work.</p> <p>A dot may use other participants' messages as context when its owner brings it into a Slack thread. Anyone with access to the conversation can see its posts. Information from another channel doesn't give the dot permission to share it with a new audience. Check recipients before posting work content.</p> <p>Microsoft Teams access is limited to an invite-only alpha.</p> <p><span id=\"does-o-always-ask-before-sending-or-changing-something\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"does-a-dot-always-ask-before-sending-or-changing-something\"></a> <strong>Does a dot always ask before sending or changing something?</strong></p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-e13354c6b025f6aa?anchor=how-action-review-works\">Auto-review</a> checks proposed actions against the user's instructions, custom rules, and safety requirements. Asking a dot to draft a message doesn't give it permission to send it. See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001495-managing-app-permissions-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">app permissions (online)</a> for approval options.</p> <p><span id=\"how-should-we-stop-work-or-remove-a-users-access\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"how-do-admins-revoke-dots-access\"></a> <strong>How do admins revoke dots access?</strong></p> <p>See <a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46?anchor=manage-access-changes\">Manage access changes</a> for steps to remove access and check connected accounts, computers, and ongoing work.</p> <p><span id=\"how-do-custom-rules-affect-confirmations\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"how-do-custom-rules-affect-confirmations\"></a> <strong>How do custom rules affect confirmations?</strong></p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-e13354c6b025f6aa?anchor=set-custom-rules\">Custom dot rules</a> guide when a dot acts or asks for confirmation. If you turn them off, members can't add or edit rules, and saved rules won't apply. The dot still follows default rules and the user's instructions.</p> <p>Custom rules don't grant tool access or override workspace permissions and built-in safety requirements. Turning them off also doesn't make the dot ask before every action. Check capability and app approval settings to control what it can do.</p> <p><span id=\"what-safeguards-help-protect-work-done-by-dots\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"what-safeguards-help-protect-work-done-by-dots\"></a> <strong>What safeguards help protect work done by dots?</strong></p> <p>Built-in safeguards help defend against malicious instructions and can pause or stop work when monitoring detects a safety concern.</p> <p>Members can follow progress in <a href=\"#/article/a-e13354c6b025f6aa?anchor=review-work\">Activity View</a>, redirect work, and check results before using them.</p> <h3 id=\"models-and-usage\">Models and usage</h3> <p><span id=\"do-existing-model-controls-and-defaults-apply-to-o\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"do-existing-model-controls-and-defaults-apply-to-dots\"></a> <strong>Do existing model controls and defaults apply to dots?</strong></p> <p>Enterprise model controls and defaults do not apply to the main dot. Tasks it delegates to Work or Codex follow those products' permissions and controls. Check dots permissions and the settings for Work and Codex when configuring access.</p> <p><a id=\"how-should-admins-monitor-adoption-and-usage\"></a> <strong>How should admins monitor adoption and usage?</strong></p> <p>Use the <a href=\"#/article/a-88b1ced5fbccd242\">Analytics API</a> to see who is using dots. Tasks a dot starts or manages in Work or Codex count toward those products' usage limits and appear in their reporting. Include those tasks when reviewing usage, and check current plan terms when setting budgets. See <a href=\"#/article/a-ba100f6664b7be87\">Work usage and cost</a> for the available controls.</p> <p>The daily usage endpoint <code>/v1/analytics/workspaces/{workspace_id}/usage</code> identifies dots with <code>client_id = DOTS</code> and supports per-user or workspace-level reporting.</p> <p><span id=\"which-data-policies-should-we-review-for-o\"></span></p> <h3 id=\"data-and-compliance\">Data and compliance</h3> <p>OpenAI does not use ChatGPT Enterprise data to improve its models by default. For OpenAI’s business data commitments, see <a href=\"https://openai.com/enterprise-privacy/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Enterprise privacy (online)</a>.</p> <p><span id=\"what-does-o-remember-between-requests\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"what-does-a-dot-remember-between-requests\"></a> <strong>What does a dot remember between requests?</strong></p> <p>A dot keeps its own context, separate from ChatGPT Memory. Turning off ChatGPT Memory stops memory sharing with the dot, but doesn't erase information it already has. Disconnecting a plugin stops future access through that connection; it doesn't remove information the dot has retained.</p> <p>Deleting a dot removes its own context. Files, Codex threads, and ChatGPT conversations it created are stored separately and aren't all deleted with it. Follow the deletion steps for each location.</p> <p>See the <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001529-dots-privacy-security-and-safety-faqs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">dots privacy FAQ (online)</a> for what is retained and deleted, and <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001530-getting-started-with-your-dot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Getting started with your dot (online)</a> for the member’s Pause and Reset controls.</p> <p><span id=\"how-can-admins-investigate-work-o-has-done\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"how-can-admins-investigate-work-a-dot-has-done\"></a> <strong>How can admins investigate work a dot has done?</strong></p> <p>Members can follow their dot's work in Activity View. Admins can use <a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0?anchor=confirm-the-administration-boundaries\">Compliance API</a> records to investigate user messages and dots' replies. Check which records are available before relying on exports for an audit, DLP, legal hold, or e-discovery.</p> <p>Supported dots records are available through the Compliance Logs Platform, including user prompts and responses, supported tool-call events, and connected-app MCP calls and results. Records identify the user and workspace; dots-attributed records use <code>client_id = DOTS</code>, and the agent object includes the dot ID, name, and type when available.</p> <p>Workspace owners or admins can select their workspace in Admin Console, then open <strong>Credentials &gt; Admin keys</strong> and create a key with the appropriate available permissions: <code>enterprise.analytics.usage.read</code> for unified usage reporting, or <code>CODEX_LOG</code> access for dots compliance records. Only workspace owners can grant broad compliance or <strong>Conversation messages</strong> access where supported. Use the <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/public/admin/api-reference\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin API reference (online)</a> to list and download compliance JSONL files and select records with <code>client_id = DOTS</code>.</p> <h2 id=\"manage-access-changes\">Manage access changes</h2> <p>When someone changes roles or leaves, check their dot's permissions, connections, and ongoing work:</p> <ol> <li><strong>Remove dots access.</strong> Check the workspace default and every role assigned directly or through groups. Remove each permission that grants access; any remaining grant can keep it enabled.</li> <li><strong>Check connected accounts and devices.</strong> Review plugin authorizations, website sessions, local computer access, and the dot's Slack identity. Each has its own settings.</li> <li><strong>Decide what happens to ongoing work.</strong> Check active tasks, recurring schedules, and tasks delegated to Work or Codex. Decide what should stop and who should take over any remaining responsibilities.</li> <li><strong>Delete data where needed.</strong> Access changes and deletion are separate steps. Follow the deletion process for the dot's context and any files or tasks stored elsewhere.</li> </ol> <p>For adding and removing workspace members, see <a href=\"#/article/a-16cf27f48eb09b1c\">User lifecycle management</a>. For dots access removal, see <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001554-manage-dots-in-chatgpt-workspaces\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Manage dots in ChatGPT workspaces (online)</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"respond-to-an-unexpected-action\">Respond to an unexpected action</h3> <p>Ask the member to pause their dot and review the affected task. Save the task link and available activity records, check the app or computer permissions involved, and follow your organization's incident process. Whether you can undo an action depends on the action and the service. See the <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001529-dots-privacy-security-and-safety-faqs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">privacy and safety FAQ (online)</a> for how to report an issue.</p> <h2 id=\"help-members-work-well-with-dots\">Help members work well with dots</h2> <p>Help members choose work to delegate and connect the accounts and tools they'll need. Encourage them to tell their dot what to do, when to do it, and who should see the result.</p> <p>For example, “Prepare a weekly project update for me to review” asks for a draft. “Post the approved update in our team channel every Friday” also gives permission to post. Members should check important results and know how to review activity, change a schedule, and pause their dot. Share <a href=\"#/article/a-7c8e52e0c73fc7d7\">Getting started</a>, <a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2\">Tasks and memory</a>, and <a href=\"#/article/a-e13354c6b025f6aa\">Controls</a> to help them get started.</p>"};
